# A copy of a spell is put onto the stack with the original's targets (CR 707.10), and each object it targets becomes a
# target of the copy - once, however many instances of "target" chose it (CR 115.3, 601.2c). Bot1 casts Trash the Town at
# its own Bonecrusher Giant with two modes (counters and trample), then Lutri, the Spellchaser copies it and Bot1 keeps both
# of the copy's targets on the Giant. The Giant becomes the target of two spells, once each: two triggers, 4 damage to Bot1,
# not 8. Both spells resolve: four counters and trample.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Bonecrusher Giant
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Trash the Town
Lutri, the Spellchaser
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x16

